1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,418
We can consider these axioms right here, which define Peano Arithmetic,

2
00:00:03,518 --> 00:00:06,788
which essentially just describe the number line. Which would be fine

3
00:00:06,888 --> 00:00:09,216
if math stopped around grade 3, but if we want to

4
00:00:09,316 --> 00:00:11,693
be able to describe all of math, we will need more

5
00:00:11,793 --> 00:00:14,815
than just the natural numbers with addition and multiplication.

6
00:00:14,866 --> 00:00:16,673
This is where set theory comes in.

7
00:00:16,733 --> 00:00:20,318
Everything in math can be seen as a set, obviously numbers are

8
00:00:20,418 --> 00:00:24,003
sets, but also functions are sets of pairs, graphs are sets of

9
00:00:24,103 --> 00:00:27,212
points and edges and even proofs are sets of formulas.

10
00:00:28,866 --> 00:00:31,872
So, if we can define what is, and what is not a valid set,

11
00:00:31,972 --> 00:00:35,245
then we will have defined what is and what is not part of math.

12
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,797
But a set is so basic, that is hard to define. If

13
00:00:37,897 --> 00:00:40,885
you try to define a set, you will likely say something like

14
00:00:40,985 --> 00:00:43,973
a collection of things or a class of objects. But then, how

15
00:00:44,073 --> 00:00:46,904
do you define a collection or a class? The axioms of ZFC

16
00:00:47,004 --> 00:00:49,992
are a good attempt to precisely define the notion of a set.

17
00:00:50,066 --> 00:00:53,571
Now, when we want to start defining the set theory, we run into

18
00:00:53,671 --> 00:00:58,262
a fundamental issue with definitions. Words are defined using other words, so when

19
00:00:58,362 --> 00:01:01,524
we want to define the first word, what do we do? So there

20
00:01:01,624 --> 00:01:05,300
has to be some sort of a-priori assumptions, which are the axioms.

21
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:09,024
The first axiom we will look at, is the axiom of existence, which

22
00:01:09,124 --> 00:01:13,001
simply asserts that there is some set. Specifically, that there is a set

23
00:01:13,101 --> 00:01:16,261
with no members, the so called empty set. So at the base of

24
00:01:16,361 --> 00:01:20,349
this whole set theoretic Universe, is that assumption that nothing exists.

25
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,476
We know that the emptyset is unique, due to

26
00:01:22,576 --> 00:01:25,260
the axiom of extensionality, which just states that two

27
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:27,588
sets are equal iff they have the same members.

28
00:01:27,666 --> 00:01:30,997
Once we have sets, we can define other sets, for example using

29
00:01:31,097 --> 00:01:34,428
the pairing axiom, which just states that given two sets X and

30
00:01:34,528 --> 00:01:36,918
Y, we can form a set with X and Y as members.

31
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,714
Applying this with the empty set with itself, gives us the

32
00:01:39,814 --> 00:01:42,772
set containing the emptyset. So, we start with nothing, then we

33
00:01:42,872 --> 00:01:44,859
can put a bag around it and so we no longer

34
00:01:44,959 --> 00:01:47,140
have nothing, we have a bag with nothing in it.

35
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:50,625
This is obviously pretty dumb, but we are essentially defining

36
00:01:50,725 --> 00:01:53,923
the natural numbers. The emptyset is 0, the set containing

37
00:01:54,023 --> 00:01:56,425
the empty set is 1, and then from here, just

38
00:01:56,525 --> 00:01:59,496
like Russian Dolls, we will define the successor to be

39
00:01:59,596 --> 00:02:02,851
the set of all predecessors. Which requires the union axiom

40
00:02:05,466 --> 00:02:08,333
So, we can define 2 as the set containing 0 and

41
00:02:08,433 --> 00:02:10,922
1. Then 3 as the set with 0,1 and 2. Then

42
00:02:11,022 --> 00:02:15,214
we can continue this indefinitely, resulting in the ordinal numbers.

43
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:20,677
The ordinals, which are essentially just the natural numbers, will form the spine

44
00:02:20,777 --> 00:02:24,569
of the set theoretic Universe. We will use the following axiom, known as

45
00:02:24,669 --> 00:02:27,271
the power set axiom to define the rest of the sets

